  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A sealed cylinder contains neon <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\left ( _{10}^{20}\\textrm{Ne} \\right )\"></span> gas and argon <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\left ( _{18}^{40}\\textrm{Ar} \\right )\"></span> gas molecules. The average speed of the neon gas molecules is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v_{n}\"></span> and the average speed of the argon gas molecules is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"v_{a}\"></span>. All the molecules in the cylinder have the same temperature. What is the ratio of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{v_{a}}{v_{n}}\"></span>?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sqrt{2}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
